  "body": {
    "id": "lem:exact-score-split",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_{2,\\mathrm{loc}}\\), \\(Z_i^{(w)}-\\tau_{\\mathrm P}=\\xi_i^{(w)}+h_i\\) and \\(\\mathbb E_P[\\xi_i^{(w)}h_j]=0\\) for all \\(i,j\\in\\mathbb Z\\) and \\(w\\in\\{1,2\\}\\). In addition, \\(|Z_i^{(w)}|\\le K\\) almost surely.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M_{2,\\mathrm{loc}}\\)",
      "\\(Z_i^{(1)}\\)",
      "\\(Z_i^{(2)}\\)",
      "\\(\\tau_{\\mathrm P}\\)",
      "\\(\\xi_i^{(1)}\\)",
      "\\(\\xi_i^{(2)}\\)",
      "\\(h_i\\)",
      "\\(K\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:two-wave-local-class",
      "def:score-decomposition"
    ],
    "justification": "The decomposition retains the sound assignment--environment split and supplies the common envelope required for a uniform diagnostic.",
    "gap": "AbadieAtheyImbensWooldridge2020 separates sampling and design uncertainty without repeated local exposure-IPW scores; Leung2022ANI works conditionally on one realized finite population.",
    "consumer": "The split identifies which cross-wave products eliminate assignment noise and which envelope controls finite-sample error.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_{2,\\mathrm{loc}}\\).  For either \\(w\\in\\{1,2\\}\\), the score-decomposition definitions give\n\\[\n \\xi_i^{(w)}+h_i=(Z_i^{(w)}-m_i)+(m_i-\\tau_{\\mathrm P})\n =Z_i^{(w)}-\\tau_{\\mathrm P}. \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThe definition \\(m_i=\\mathbb E_P[Z_i^{(w)}\\mid\\mathcal F_U]\\) implies\n\\(\\mathbb E_P[\\xi_i^{(w)}\\mid\\mathcal F_U]=0\\).  Because \\(h_j\\) is \\(\\mathcal F_U\\)-measurable, the pull-out and tower properties of conditional expectation yield\n\\[\n \\mathbb E_P[\\xi_i^{(w)}h_j]\n =\\mathbb E_P\\!\\left[h_j\\mathbb E_P(\\xi_i^{(w)}\\mid\\mathcal F_U)\\right]=0. \\tag{2}\n\\]\nAll terms are integrable by the following envelope calculation.  If \\(e_1\\ne e_0\\), at most one of the two exposure indicators in the IPW bracket is one.  The outcome envelope and exposure positivity therefore give\n\\[\n |Z_i^{(w)}|\n \\le \\frac{|Y_i(D^{(w)};U,G)|}{\\min\\{\\pi_i(e_1),\\pi_i(e_0)\\}}\n \\le \\frac B\\varepsilon=K \\qquad P\\text{-almost surely}. \\tag{3}\n\\]\nIf \\(e_1=e_0\\), the two terms in the bracket cancel and (3) is immediate.  In particular the scores, their conditional means, and all variables in (1)--(2) are square-integrable.",
